Z||000000||SCCA FIERO||08-25-2001||08:52 PM||||Trying to get eveything working on my Fiero here...<P>I replaced the servo and checked the can for leaks (I unplugged a hose and the air came out after I did that). I assume there are no leaks.<P>Then I checked the pedal switches. The one for the clutch was not even touching the tab on the pedal. I pushed it in until it touched the pedal. When I did that (with key on) I can hear a click coming from somewhere. I just went out and found out where the click was coming from, it's coming from the part on the servo that has the 2 plug going to it (not sure what it is). But when I plug and unplg that plug, it makes a sound. Just thought I would add that to help...<P>I don't have an extra stalk laying around to test...<P>Any thoughts?<p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||08-25-2001||10:43 PM||||Nevermind... I fixed it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GWMORGAN||08-25-2001||11:03 PM||||What was the problem and how did you fix it?||||reg||1
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||08-27-2001||08:09 PM||||I actually wasn't pushing the button (on the stalk) long enough I guess. But the problem was the clutch switch - it wasn't touching the pedal at all. When this was adjusted I could hear the servo click when I turned the cruise on, with the key to "run".||||reg||1
Z||000004||stsmithgt||08-28-2001||10:02 AM||||That clutch switch seems to get beat the most.  I had to take mine apart when I first bought my car and tighten up the pressure of the contacts with a little force beside only adjusting it.||||reg||1
